A||N||4||SloPonti||Need help with Poly bushings for the 84 front control arms-thrush washer||||5||
Z||000000||SloPonti||04-20-2001||06:22 PM||||i am replacing the control arm bushings in the front upper and lower control arms with poly-i have everything off the car and i have the old bushings burned out of the old sleave! i see the kit from the fiero store gives you thrush washers for the lower control arm! my question is-do we use these bushings? they fit onto the poly bushing but when the bushing is in the control arm they do not? thanks for your help in advanced!!<BR>Rob||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||04-20-2001||06:27 PM||||I am not aware of any thrust washers for the lower control arms.  <P>The upper control arms use washers betwwen the bushing and the nut on each side.  Could they be intended for the upper control arm?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||04-20-2001||06:28 PM||||Hey Rob!<BR>When I did my 84, I did not get washers...<BR>Best guess, leave em out if they don't fit...<BR>Or use one if there is slack...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||04-20-2001||06:52 PM||||By thrust washers, do you mean four doughnut shaped poly disks?<P>When I did the LCA's on my 85, these disks went on the inboard side of each of the bushings. They didn't take up any more room installed since they fit over the outer sleeve and the extra bit of poly bushing that sticks out the far side. Here's how they go:<P>Bolt-Frame-Bushing-A arm-Disk-Frame-Nut-Space-Nut-Frame-Disk-A arm-Bushing-Frame-Bolt<P>------------------<BR>85 SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||04-22-2001||02:45 AM||||The kit I got from the Fiero Store didn't have any thrust washers.<P>Do they look like they are supposed to replace the washers for the upper arm?  Not sure how you'd get them in for the lower control arm as I had to tunk the LCA with a rubber mallot to get it back on the car.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
